PolarKEM-512 -- reference implementation
=========================================

Profile
-------

    Public key:     4096 bytes
    Private key:    8192 bytes
    Ciphertext:     2304 bytes
    Shared secret:    64 bytes
    Modulus q:     18433
    Instance ID:    0x05
    Quantization:      8 bits/coefficient

This directory implements the fixed functional-evaluation profile described in
the rectification report.  It activates only Construction D level 0, fixes all
higher-level coefficients to zero, and does not use an NTT.  The exact signed
permutation is deterministically expanded from the 32-byte public transform
seed.  These choices are intended for reproducible implementation evaluation;
the frozen submission paper and rectification report remain the normative
sources for design rationale and security analysis.

Contents
--------

KEM_AlgorithmInstance.c/h provides the official API_PKC interface.  KAT_KEM.c,
auxfunc.c/h, and drng.c/h are byte-for-byte copies of the official API_PKC
distribution.  polarkem_core.c/h implements KeyGen, encapsulation,
decapsulation, serialization, full-ciphertext recomputation, and implicit
rejection.  polarkem_polar.c/h contains the no-bit-reversal GF(2) Polar
transform and deterministic signed permutation.  polarkem_pack.c/h contains
coefficient quantization and bit packing.  polarkem_ct.c/h contains
constant-time comparison and object-header validation.  polarkem_params.h fixes
all instance dimensions and offsets.

Build and run
-------------

POSIX/GNU-compatible make:

    make clean all
    make run
    make sanitizer

Windows with GCC on PATH:

    build.bat
    KAT_KEM.exe
    build.bat sanitize
    build.bat clean

The strict build uses -std=c99 -Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic -Werror.  The official
KAT writes ten populated records to output/KAT_KEM_PolarKEM-512.txt.

In sanitizer builds, KAT_KEM.c and every project-owned translation unit receive
full ASan/UBSan instrumentation.  The exact official auxfunc.c and drng.c also
remain instrumented, with only the known shift check disabled because their
upstream SM3 rotate macro contains a shift-by-32 expression.  The official
files remain unmodified.

Official API behavior
---------------------

The four length getters return the fixed byte lengths above.  kem_keygen,
kem_enc, and kem_dec return 0 on success.  -1 is reserved for ciphertext
rejection and still returns a full-length implicit-rejection shared secret.
-2 reports a null pointer; -3 reports an incorrect caller-supplied input length
or a non-canonical public/private-key serialization; and -4 reports a failure
of the official DRNG, SM3, or pseudoXOF primitive.  Output lengths are zero on
failure except for -1.

Evaluation scope / 评估范围
---------------------------

This README records the instance parameters, implementation files, build
procedure, and official API behavior.  Algorithm design rationale and security
analysis are defined by the frozen submission paper and rectification report.

本 README 说明实例参数、实现文件、构建方法和官方接口行为。算法设计依据与
安全性分析以冻结的算法文本及整改说明为准。
